    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification asked for an `initials` field on the owner: the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern for the analogous computed `displayName` field:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema, right beside `displayName`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient` `getInitials()` getter next to `getDisplayName()`, with a small private `initial(String)` helper (single responsibility, no duplication). MapStruct auto-maps `getInitials()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.initials` by name, so no controller or mapper changes were needed.\n\nI placed the logic on `Owner` alongside the pre-existing `getDisplayName()` \u2014 the established home for owner name-formatting derivations \u2014 rather than scattering it into the controller or mapper.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` (and the whole suite) is green.",
